<resources>
    <string name="app_name">JoyMouse</string>
    <string name="accessibility_service_summary">Allows a joystick to control a virtual mouse cursor</string>
    <string name="accessibility_service_description">Allows the use of a joystick or gamepad to control a mouse cursor in order to interact with this device.</string>

    <string name="operating_instructions_section_title">Usage:</string>
    <string name="operating_instructions">Once enabled, moving the right thumbstick will move the mouse cursor. Pressing the %1$s while moving the cursor will cause it to move faster.</string>
    <string name="operating_instructions_primary_button">Pulling the %1$s will simulate a finger down. If the button is released quickly, it will emulate a tap at the cursor position. If the button is held and then released, it will act as a long press. If the button is held and the cursor is moved it will be interpreted as a drag. If the A button is pressed while dragged, the drag will be toggled to a fling gesture.</string>
    <string name="operating_instructions_toggle_chord">Pressing `LEFT SHOULDER` + `RIGHT SHOULDER` + `X` will toggle the virtual mouse on and off. While the mouse is enabled, joystick events will not be passed on to other applications.</string>
    <string name="operating_instructions_toggle_chord_template">Pressing %1$s will toggle the virtual mouse on and off. While the mouse is enabled, joystick events will not be passed on to other applications.</string>

